          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: 'Be the first player to empty your face-down row by matching tiles to the central line.',
          gameplay: '1. **Start**: A tile is drawn from the boneyard to start the line. 2. **The Turn**: On your turn, flip over the LEFTMOST face-down tile in your row. 3. **The Match**: If the tile matches either open end of the central line, you must play it. 4. **The Failure**: If the tile does not match, you must turn it face down again in its original position. 5. **Boneyard**: Unused tiles are not drawn; the game relies only on the initial hand.',
          keyRules: [
            'You must always turn the leftmost tile first.',
            'Memory is your only tool: you must remember what tiles were returned face-down.',
            'The game ends when someone goes domino (empties row) or when no one can move (blocked).',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: "Memory is essential. When you flip a tile that doesn't match, memorize its pip values. When the line ends change later, you'll know if that specific tile can be played.",
          intermediate: 'Opponent Tracking: Watch what your opponents flip and return. If they return a 5-2, and you have control over the line ends, try to make one of the ends a 5 or 2 to force them to play a tile they might not want to.',
          advanced: 'Block Prevention: If you know your leftmost tile matches an end, but playing it would change that end to a value you know your *next* tile cannot match, consider the risk of blocking yourself.',
          tips: [
            "Don't worry about strategy too much—the 'Leftmost' rule makes it highly luck-dependent.",
            'Try to keep the line ends varied to maximize your chances of a match.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
